{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#ex:dc-ch6-2-8","title":"ex:dc-ch6-2-8","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions.md","line":301,"body":"","kind":"proof","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions.tex#ex:dc-ch6-2-8","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-2-patch]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-2-B]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-2-2]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#thm:dc-ch6-2-5]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#rem:dc-ch6-2-6]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#lem:dc-ch6-2-8-euclidean-opens]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions.tex","label":"ex:dc-ch6-2-8","line":709,"source":"\\begin{example}[curvature of $S^n$]\n  \\label{ex:dc-ch6-2-8}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch6-2-patch, def:dc-ch6-2-B, def:dc-ch6-2-2, thm:dc-ch6-2-5, rem:dc-ch6-2-6, lem:dc-ch6-2-8-euclidean-opens}\n\n  \\dcref{ch6:2.8}\n  The sphere of radius $r$ in Euclidean space has constant sectional curvature\n  $1/r^2$; in particular, the unit sphere has constant sectional curvature $1$.\n\\end{example}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n  With the inward unit normal $\\eta=-p/r$, the second fundamental form is\n  $H_\\eta(x,y)=\\langle x,y\\rangle/r$, so $S_\\eta=r^{-1}\\mathrm{id}$. Gauss'\n  equation against the flat ambient gives sectional curvature $1/r^2$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p>\\begin{example} \\end{example}[curvature of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S^n$\">$S^n$</span>] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-65783a64632d6368362d322d38\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_IsometricImmersions%23def%3Adc-ch6-2-patch\">↗ def:dc-ch6-2-patch</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_IsometricImmersions%23def%3Adc-ch6-2-B\">↗ def:dc-ch6-2-B</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_IsometricImmersions%23def%3Adc-ch6-2-2\">↗ def:dc-ch6-2-2</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_IsometricImmersions%23thm%3Adc-ch6-2-5\">↗ thm:dc-ch6-2-5</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_IsometricImmersions%23rem%3Adc-ch6-2-6\">↗ rem:dc-ch6-2-6</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_IsometricImmersions%23lem%3Adc-ch6-2-8-euclidean-opens\">↗ lem:dc-ch6-2-8-euclidean-opens</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch6:2.8</span></span>The sphere of radius <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$r$\">$r$</span> in Euclidean space has constant sectional curvature <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1/r^2$\">$1/r^2$</span>; in particular, the unit sphere has constant sectional curvature <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1$\">$1$</span>. \\end{example} <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch With the inward unit normal <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\eta =-p/r$\">$\\eta =-p/r$</span>, the second fundamental form is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$H_\\eta (x,y)=\\langle x,y\\rangle /r$\">$H_\\eta (x,y)=\\langle x,y\\rangle /r$</span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S_\\eta =r^{-1}\\mathrm{id}$\">$S_\\eta =r^{-1}\\mathrm{id}$</span>. Gauss’ equation against the flat ambient gives sectional curvature <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1/r^2$\">$1/r^2$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: example、sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#lem:dc-ch6-2-8-euclidean-opens","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-2-8-geodesic","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-2-patch","title":"def:dc-ch6-2-patch","label":"def:dc-ch6-2-patch"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-2-B","title":"def:dc-ch6-2-B","label":"def:dc-ch6-2-B"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-2-2","title":"def:dc-ch6-2-2","label":"def:dc-ch6-2-2"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#thm:dc-ch6-2-5","title":"thm:dc-ch6-2-5","label":"thm:dc-ch6-2-5"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#rem:dc-ch6-2-6","title":"rem:dc-ch6-2-6","label":"rem:dc-ch6-2-6"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#lem:dc-ch6-2-8-euclidean-opens","title":"lem:dc-ch6-2-8-euclidean-opens","label":"lem:dc-ch6-2-8-euclidean-opens"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#ex:dc-ch6-2-4","title":"ex:dc-ch6-2-4","label":"ex:dc-ch6-2-4"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#ex:dc-ch6-2-8","title":"ex:dc-ch6-2-8","tex":"\\begin{example}[curvature of $S^n$]\n  \\label{ex:dc-ch6-2-8}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch6-2-patch, def:dc-ch6-2-B, def:dc-ch6-2-2, thm:dc-ch6-2-5, rem:dc-ch6-2-6, lem:dc-ch6-2-8-euclidean-opens}\n\n  \\dcref{ch6:2.8}\n  The sphere of radius $r$ in Euclidean space has constant sectional curvature\n  $1/r^2$; in particular, the unit sphere has constant sectional curvature $1$.\n\\end{example}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n  With the inward unit normal $\\eta=-p/r$, the second fundamental form is\n  $H_\\eta(x,y)=\\langle x,y\\rangle/r$, so $S_\\eta=r^{-1}\\mathrm{id}$. Gauss'\n  equation against the flat ambient gives sectional curvature $1/r^2$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-2-patch","title":"def:dc-ch6-2-patch","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-2-B","title":"def:dc-ch6-2-B","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-2-2","title":"def:dc-ch6-2-2","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#thm:dc-ch6-2-5","title":"thm:dc-ch6-2-5","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#rem:dc-ch6-2-6","title":"rem:dc-ch6-2-6","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#lem:dc-ch6-2-8-euclidean-opens","title":"lem:dc-ch6-2-8-euclidean-opens","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}